      "pageTitle": "Call for Applications: JAWS 2027 Health Journalism Fellowship — JAWS",
      "pageDescription": "Application deadline: Monday, December 7, 2026&nbsp;   $4,000 reporting stipend   Early career U.S. journalists are encouraged to   apply for the 2027 Journalism &amp; Women Symposium (JAWS) Health Journalism Fellowship  . This unique opportunity includes a $4,000 stipend, workshops, mentori",
      "evidenceText": "Call for Applications: JAWS 2027 Health Journalism Fellowship — JAWS 0 Call for Applications: JAWS 2027 Health Journalism Fellowship Oct 20 Written by Journalism & Women Symposium Application deadline: Monday, December 7, 2026  $4,000 reporting stipend Early career U.S. journalists are encouraged to apply for the 2027 Journalism & Women Symposium (JAWS) Health Journalism Fellowship . This unique opportunity includes a $4,000 stipend, workshops, mentoring and more! The fellowship is open* to women and individuals who identify as women with 2 to 7 years of professional journalism experience. This fellowship, made possible with support from The Commonwealth Fund, is in keeping with JAWS’ mission to advance the professional empowerment and personal growth of women in journalism and advocate for more inclusive coverage of the diverse experiences and cultures that comprise our society. Learn from veteran health journalists/mentors and outside experts while you report and produce an in-depth project on a key component of healthcare, including but not limited to: Health equity/disparities Cost and quality of care Healthcare coverage and access Women’s health/women’s reproductive health Delivery system reform Medicare/Medicaid The fellows will present their work at JAWS CAMP 2027, with complimentary travel expenses and registration (a $3,500 value) and receive a one-year complimentary membership to JAWS (a $75 value). Both staff reporters and independent journalists in all mediums are encouraged to apply. Questions? Contact Liz Seegert, project director, liz@jaws.com * Open to applicants within the U.S. only APPLY NOW Journalism & Women Symposium Previous Previous JAWS CAMP 2026 Photo & Video Recap Next Next JAWS Announces 2027 Board of Directors Election Winners",
