      "pageDescription": "The Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize acknowledges exceptional researchers making significant contributions to learning and development, or improving the living conditions of children and youth.",
      "evidenceText": "The Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize - Jacobs Foundation Share Content Article Link Copied Close Home Programs The Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize Programs The Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize The Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize The Klaus J. Jacobs Awards were established in 2009, in memory of our founder, to honor his commitment to promoting scientific advancement in our knowledge of how children learn and develop. The Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize acknowledges exceptional researchers who are making significant contributions in any scholarly discipline related to learning and development, or aimed at improving the living conditions of children and youth.  Visit the application page to apply today. The prize recipient receives an endowment worth 1 million Swiss Francs to support their research.  The jury  consists of a selected group of internationally renowned scientists working across a range of disciplines. See the list of previous recipients of the Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize . Criteria and Eligibility For the first time this year, researchers are invited to apply directly for the prize. Nominations of exceptional academics are also welcomed. Visit the criteria and eligibility requirements to learn more. Applications close 31 January 2027 . Explore more The Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize 2027 Apply or nominate 2025 Prize Recipient – Hirokazu Yoshikawa Learn more The Klaus J. Jacobs Research Prize – Criteria & Eligibility Learn more Share this page Copy link Share on Facebook Share on X Share on LinkedIn Share on Whatsapp Share on Email",
