      "pageTitle": "RSF Berlin Fellowship 2027: Applications Now Open | RSF Resources for Journalists",
      "pageDescription": "Reporters Without Borders (RSF) Germany will once again invite journalists from countries with restricted freedom of press and information to Berlin for our annual fellowship program. Please apply online starting November 15th, 2026 until December 15th, 2026. Reporters Without Borders (RSF) Germany will once again invite journalists from countries with&hellip;",
      "evidenceText": "RSF Berlin Fellowship 2027: Applications Now Open | RSF Resources for Journalists Reporters Without Borders (RSF) Germany will once again invite journalists from countries with restricted freedom of press and information to Berlin for our annual fellowship program. Please apply online starting November 15th, 2026 until December 15th, 2026. Reporters Without Borders (RSF) Germany will once again invite journalists from countries with restricted freedom of press and information to Berlin for our annual fellowship program. The RSF Fellowship Program is designed to provide a safe space for journalists: Fellows will be able to take time off from their daily obligations and recover from their difficult working conditions, whilst learning new skills to better protect themselves by taking part in comprehensive safety trainings program on digital security. THE FELLOWSHIP PROGRAM The 2027 RSF Fellowship Program runs from May until October and encompasses: A comprehensive, hands-on training program in digital security, including individual risk assessments and mentoring in risk mitigation strategies. Workshops on safety and resilience-building for journalists covering sensitive issues. Peer-to-peer exchange with colleagues from different regions and professional backgrounds. Insights into the activities of Reporters Without Borders, a human rights organisation active around the world. Networking opportunities with German media professionals and newsrooms. Opportunities to meet with relevant stakeholders in German civil society and policy fields. Holistic support for individual psychosocial needs. We expect fellows to be available for all program activities. Please plan to spend up to approximately 20 to 25 hours per week on training, workshops and activities. Although there will be breaks in the programme that can be individually used for travel or work purposes, it will not be possible to keep to a full-time editorial schedule while taking part in the fellowship. The fellowship aims to empower journalists to promote digital self-defence among their colleagues and networks of media professionals. After completing the fellowship, participants are expected to conduct at least one workshop or training session in their country of residence. WHAT RSF GERMANY PROPOSES In addition to the program outlined above, RSF will cover: Visa and travel expenses Assistance with all visa-related matters A furnished studio apartment in Berlin for the duration of the fellowship A monthly stipend Travel and health insurance Public transportation costs within Germany Travel to networking events and/or journalism conferences A co-working space in a Berlin media hub Touristic and social activities PERIOD OF STAY IN BERLIN The Fellowship runs from May to October 2027. The exact travel dates to and from Berlin will be coordinated with the selected participants. RSF will assist with obtaining the necessary visa. However, being selected for the program does not automatically guarantee a positive or timely visa outcome. WHO CAN APPLY: ELIGIBILITY & REQUIREMENTS The RSF Fellowship is open to working journalists with at least three years’ professional experience. This includes both full-time staff and freelancers working in any type of medium. We actively promote diversity and encourage applicants from a range of backgrounds to apply. Expectations include: Fellows are expected to openly discuss their experiences and challenges as working journalists with a group of peers from diverse backgrounds. They should also share the knowledge they acquire during the programme with their colleagues back home. After completing the fellowship, participants are expected to return to their home region or country of residence (including third countries of permanent residence). The program will be conducted entirely in English, so fluency in speaking, reading and writing English is required in order to participate fully. Please be aware that: The RSF Fellowship is open to applicants from any country who are at significant risk due to their journalistic work. However, applicants must be able to demonstrate that they could return to their country of residence at the end of the fellowship period for visa application purposes. RSF can only support journalists working in independent media; those working in government or politically affiliated media workers will not be considered. Applicants working as investigative journalists on topics related to human rights, such as climate change, corruption, labour rights or migration, will be given positive consideration in the selection process. To apply, candidates will be asked to address the following: Their experiences of threats or persecution, and how these relate directly to their journalistic activity. Concrete ideas demonstrating how the fellowship will positively impact their current work situation. They should also describe the type of digital threats they encounter and explain how digital security training would impact their personal safety, as well as that of their colleagues and sources. THE TRAINING PROGRAM FOR DIGITAL SELF-DEFENSE A main goal of the program will be to improve the participants’ digital security. Fellows should demonstrate a strong interest in developing an in-depth understanding of digital safety for journalists. However, a high level of existing proficiency in digital security is not required.The application is open to anyone who is familiar with using computers and smartphones. Topics covered in the workshops include: Operational security, including risk assessments and security planning Online identity management for investigative journalists, including the technical background and practical use of anonymization tools Secure online communication concepts, technology and tools, including secure online conferencing for interviews Password and account security and data protection for social media and other online accounts used for media work Device security for the computers and mobile phones of journalists at risk Website security for media websites under attack Secure online and offline data storage including encryption for media files Open Source Intelligence (OSINT) Concepts against digital violence, including online gender-based violence, doxxing, impersonation and trolling Safe use of AI for media professionals, including the protection of sensitive data and the use of AI assistants as tools for developing security concepts HOW TO APPLY If you match the eligibility criteria outlined above, you can apply for the RSF Fellowship Program until December 15th, 2026. Please register and fill out the online application form and upload the required documents here .Please be prepared to submit the following: A completed online application form A scan of your passport CV Contact information for two professional references The deadline for applications is Tuesday, December 15th, 2026 at 12:00 PM (CET). PARTNERS & COOPERATIONS The RSF BERLIN FELLOWSHIP PROGRAM is funded by the Berlin Senate Department for Economic Affairs, Energy and Public Enterprises , as well as the generous support of Reporters without Borders Germany’s members and donors. Latest Posts What to do when your device is seized Online content takedowns in India: dealing with legal pressure and self-censorship Online content takedowns: 10 practical recommendations for journalists The Propaganda Monitor Toolkit: resources for journalists How the Kremlin uses disinformation to push its narrative Navigating Interrogations in China (Part 2): 20 Practical Rules for Journalists Interrogated in China Navigating Interrogations in China (Part 1): Key insights about the interrogation system RSF Berlin Fellowship 2027: Applications Now Open",
