      "title": "As Democrats swept the midterms, news anchors struggled to find the words",
      "url": "https://awfulannouncing.com/espn/joe-scarborough-pat-mcafee-college-gameday.html",
      "category": "uncategorized",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T23:44:07.796Z",
      "httpStatus": 200,
      "finalUrl": "https://awfulannouncing.com/espn/joe-scarborough-pat-mcafee-college-gameday.html",
      "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
      "pageTitle": "Joe Scarborough sick of ESPN letting Pat McAfee ruin GameDay",
      "pageDescription": "Forget about politicians ruining the country, Joe Scarborough used Election Day to put Pat McAfee on blast for running College GameDay.",
      "evidenceText": "Joe Scarborough sick of ESPN letting Pat McAfee ruin GameDay Skip to content Credit: USA TODAY Network via Reuters Connect, MS NOW By Brandon Contes on 11/03/2026 11/03/2026 Less AI and more AA in your search results. Forget about politicians ruining the country, Joe Scarborough took a few minutes on Election Day to put Pat McAfee on blast for running College GameDay . Tuesday morning’s Election Day coverage on MS NOW’s Morning Joe was briefly usurped by football with Willie Geist discussing ESPN’s six-part documentary, Saban , which was produced by his sister Libby Geist. And while they were on the topic of football, Scarborough had to get something off his chest about ESPN and Pat McAfee. It’s election day in America, and Morning Joe spent over two minutes discussing the country’s most pressing issue: Pat McAfee ruining College GameDay “I don’t know if they haven’t gotten the message yet, but the manosphere that we all thought was brought in in ’24, it may get washed aside” — Awful Announcing (@awfulannouncing) November 3, 2026 “While we’re talking football, does anybody want to get in trouble? I’ll just say it myself,” Scarborough began. “I’ve just had enough of this Pat McAfee ruining College GameDay . I look forward to waking up on Saturday mornings and watching that. And I don’t know if they haven’t got the message yet, but the manosphere that we all thought was brought in in ’24, it may get washed aside. “Maybe you weren’t having to be [grunt noise] and yelling at people and being freaked out because two kids in Utah put up signs or say something that might offend you.” Scarborough said he loves watching Nick Saban, he enjoys listening to Rece Davis, he praised Desmond Howard for being great and even called Kirk Herbstreit “amazing.” But that Pat McAfee guy? Not so much. “They’re all great,” Scarborough insisted of everyone on College GameDay not named Pat McAfee. “And they’re all being eclipsed by ESPN’s insatiable desire to give this guy more time.” Once an aspiring WFAN host , always an aspiring WFAN host, because even Election Day coverage couldn’t stop Scarborough from dropping a sports rant Tuesday morning. ESPN built its relationship with McAfee through GameDay , with the former NFL punter joining the Worldwide Leader’s premier college football show as a full-time analyst in 2022. And McAfee’s addition has led to ratings success, which is part of why ESPN has gone all in on continuing to make him the face of their network. Despite ESPN’s affinity for McAfee, Scarborough isn’t alone in growing tired of the partnership. Part of it is ESPN’s fault for seeking to get their money’s worth on the $65 million per year contract extension they’re reportedly signing McAfee to. But ESPN audiences seeing McAfee on his weekday show, GameDay , Monday Night Countdown and his Monday Night Football alt-cast is becoming too much McAfee for some sports fans to handle. McAfee is a natural entertainer and a very successful sports show host. But he continues to do himself no favors by being overly sensitive to criticism and vengeful of those who criticize him. His feud with the University of Utah stemming from McAfee losing it over a student accusing him of being likely to “ say something corny ” has only pushed more sports fans and media critics to Scarborough’s side of the McAfee debate. About Brandon Contes Brandon Contes is a staff writer for Awful Announcing and The Comeback. He previously helped carve the sports vertical for Mediaite and spent more than three years with Barrett Sports Media. Send tips/comments/complaints to bcontes@thecomeback.com View all posts by Brandon Contes Follow on Twitter Related Content The WNBA has figured out the best way to handle manufactured outrage: ignore it Who will land the 2030 FIFA World Cup rights? Nostalgia, personality, and community: Was sports media at its best when highlights were scarce? Five players who deserved to win the Heisman Trophy but didn't Recent Posts \"There always seems to be smoke around Aaron Rodgers.\" Colin Cowherd must not watch a lot of college football if he doesn't think the Texas State Bobcats are a real school. There was no reason for Cody Campbell to ask a question at Joey McGuire's postgame press conference, but who's going to stop him? \"Nobody wins when the family feuds.\" NBC highlighted Browns linebacker Carson Schwesinger rather than Deshaun Watson to promote the game's appearance on Sunday Night Football . \"I hope this is one time he's telling the truth.\" Sidebar Popular Posts The top five candidates to replace Ernie Johnson on ‘Inside the NBA’ Corned beef, Cheerwine, and carving stations: Ranking every NHL team’s media meals Recent Posts \"There always seems to be smoke around Aaron Rodgers.\" Colin Cowherd must not watch a lot of college football if he doesn't think the Texas State Bobcats are a real school. There was no reason for Cody Campbell to ask a question at Joey McGuire's postgame press conference, but who's going to stop him? \"Nobody wins when the family feuds.\" NBC highlighted Browns linebacker Carson Schwesinger rather than Deshaun Watson to promote the game's appearance on Sunday Night Football . \"I hope this is one time he's telling the truth.\"",
