r 2) Focus on cost of living/inflation 3) Put America First 4) Change our relationship to Israel Our voters showed up. And the above four reasons are why many of them voted for Democrats. This is according to a pollster who nailed the results. While many spent Monday attacking Rachel Campos Duffy for calling for a diplomatic resolution to the conflict, it turns out her political advice was sound. (She’s also a great person.) In the next few months, there's going to be a lot of gaslighting. Expect to hear any number of establishment politicians say the solution to our woes is amnesty. I'm open to the idea that we should change enforcement—by focusing more on businesses that hire illegal labor, for instance. But anyone pushing amnesty is lying to you. The reason we lost is the war. The president himself said so last night. If you'd like to argue it was worth it, that losing the Senate for the next 6 years was worth it, then do so. Argue it was a worthwhile cost to pay. Agree or disagree, that's at least honest. But everyone knows why we lost. And any honest conversation about where we go from here must start there. I remain hopeful about our country. To the people who are pissed off and want to say, “I told you so”: you’re right, you did tell us so. Take that energy into electing Republicans who share your worldview. To the people who are just pissed at the results, you should be. Let’s take that anger and get back to the work of saving our country. 3:38 PM · Nov 4, 2026 · 73.7M Views 69K 52K 284K 68K connor @ConnorEatsPants Nov 4 worst suicide note i’ve ever read but good decision regardless 123 6.6K 173K 2.3M Thomas Massie @RepThomasMassie Nov 4 Thanks for acknowledging these things. Better late than never. I’ll send you the hat. 1.8K 7.1K 128K 3.5M Jared Washington @JaredFisher1112 Nov 4 You didn’t lose because of the war. You lost because you’re part of a regime that’s been acting like an authoritarian group of fascists for the past two years. And America fucking 